WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.440
What do giant squirrels have to do with Norse&nbsp;
mythology? Our last look at Thor: Love and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.400
Thunder before the film’s release contains some&nbsp;
small details that may point towards the answer.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.240
At the dawn of July, the&nbsp;
studio dropped a final trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.600
just in case anyone forgot that Thor is slated&nbsp;
to do glorious battle with a former Batman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:25.280
(yes, that means Christian Bale) one week later&nbsp;
on July 8th. The blockbuster, which also stars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.960
Tessa Thompson and Natalie Portman, has released&nbsp;
trailer after trailer over the past few months&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.880
with the same level of consistency as an arthouse&nbsp;
film desperately afraid of underexposure. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.600
okay, though, because it looks great, and no one&nbsp;
minds seeing more of Portman's ripped biceps.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.640
Rather contentiously, both "Avengers:&nbsp;
Infinity War" and particularly "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.680
Endgame" opted to drag Thor through every&nbsp;
possible pain he could experience (and that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:57.920
after seeing his entire world wiped out in "Thor:&nbsp;
Ragnarok," plus losing each of his parents). Most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.640
of his remaining people were slain by Thanos&nbsp;
pre-snap, his friend Heimdall [HIGHM-doll] was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.320
unceremoniously murdered by Thanos, and his&nbsp;
brother Loki was strangled by Thanos — the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.200
purple space dictator really had it out for the&nbsp;
"Thor" franchise, for some reason — and then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:18.400
the latter film proceeded to portray his journey&nbsp;
through the aforementioned pain as a joke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.040
because it's apparently hilarious to see someone&nbsp;
turn to food and drink for emotional support.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.320
Fortunately, "Thor: Love and Thunder" doesn't seem&nbsp;
to be playing the Thunder God's grief for laughs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.520
Near the start of the newest trailer, viewers&nbsp;
are treated to a somber slideshow of people that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:39.760
Thor has lost, including Frigga, his mother. Over&nbsp;
the course of these images, Gorr the God Butcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:45.600
ominously commiserates with Thor, acknowledging&nbsp;
the true depth of his loss. In addition to this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.400
it looks as if Thor is desperately attempting&nbsp;
to get his life together using meditation, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:57.040
strict workout regimen, and other ostensibly solid&nbsp;
coping mechanisms. Despite the fact that director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.520
Taika Waititi [TIE-kuh why-TEE-tee] is known for&nbsp;
trolling anyone and anything he possibly can, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.080
appears as if he's tackling Thor's mental health&nbsp;
with all the severity such a topic requires.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.880
In previous trailers, viewers were treated&nbsp;
to the fact that Thor is clearly still in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.920
love with Jane Foster who is now the Mighty&nbsp;
Thor with her ridiculously cool shattered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.720
Mjolnir [MYUL-neer]. That, along with the title&nbsp;
of the film, has long suggested that Thor's newest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:26.000
movie will heavily, or at least partially, revolve&nbsp;
around his swooning heart. In this, the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.960
recent trailer, there's a quick glimpse of the&nbsp;
two Thors holding hands. Well, sort of. They're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.240
actually doing the "holding pinky fingers" thing,&nbsp;
which is arguably the cutest way to hold hands.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:40.960
Since it's in the same black and white scale that&nbsp;
the well publicized battle with Gorr is in, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:46.160
probably a moment of camaraderie between the two&nbsp;
as they mentally prepare to fight for their lives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:51.680
After all, anyone known as the God Butcher would&nbsp;
probably stir a bit of tension in a pair of Thors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:57.040
so it might simply be them reaching out for some&nbsp;
small modicum of comfort. With that dark thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.760
in mind, it's still an incredibly tender,&nbsp;
loving gesture that's rarely seen in cinema,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.720
let alone being utilized by shredded Norse&nbsp;
deities. It's just really, really touching.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.760
Previous "Love and Thunder" trailers have&nbsp;
notably played with imagery associated with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.800
Yggrasil [IG-druh-zill], the&nbsp;
World Tree of Norse mythology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.360
and this final release again teases these&nbsp;
connections. More specifically, there's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:24.160
shot in the most recent trailer in which Mighty&nbsp;
Thor, who's holding the lightning bolt of Zeus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.360
looks as if she's sharing the bolt's power. She&nbsp;
could also be slowly murdering all those people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:34.640
who's to say? The camera angle viewers get is&nbsp;
an overhead shot that depicts the bolt spreading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:39.600
through the crowd in an interesting pattern&nbsp;
that kind of looks like the aforementioned tree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:45.440
a detail that studious fans of Norse mythology&nbsp;
have almost certainly already taken note of.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:50.320
To be fair, this particular resemblance could&nbsp;
be entirely unintentional, but assuming that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:56.000
she's sharing power and not doing a murder, the&nbsp;
symbolism would be significant. Yggdrasil is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.560
magical tree that functions like connective&nbsp;
tissue between the realms. One could climb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:05.120
the tree to get from Midgard (Earth's realm) to&nbsp;
Nifflheim [NIH-ful-hym] (Loki's original realm),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.320
provided that Ratatoskr [rat-uh-TASK-ur]&nbsp;
was cool with it (Oh, you don't know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:14.080
Ratatoskr? That's a giant squirrel beast that&nbsp;
guards Yggdrasil. Norse mythology is wild).

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:20.080
Aside from the squirrelly tangent, using&nbsp;
world tree symbology as a visual unifier is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.680
well ... it's not a deep cut,&nbsp;
but it's incredibly interesting.

